# WN22-CC-000330: Windows Server 2022 File Explorer shell protocol must run in protected mode.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-cc-000330-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 File Explorer shell protocol must run in protected mode.`
    description `The shell protocol will limit the set of folders that applications can open when run in protected mode. Restricting files an application can open to a limited set of folders increases the security of Windows.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,medium,ksi-cmt-lmc,ksi-cmt-rmv,ksi-mla-evc,ksi-svc-acm`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CMT-LMC,KSI:KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI:KSI-MLA-EVC,KSI:KSI-SVC-ACM,NIST-800-53:CM-6`
    control_objective `KSI-CMT-LMC,KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI-MLA-EVC,KSI-SVC-ACM`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `The default behavior is for shell protected mode to be turned on for File Explorer. If this needs to be corrected, configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Windows Components >> File Explorer >> Turn off shell protocol protected mode to "Not Configured" or "Disabled".`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_KSI_CMT_LMC `Windows Server implements KSI-CMT-LMC by setting registry value 'PreXPSP2ShellProtocolBehavior' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\Explorer' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_CMT_RMV `Windows Server implements KSI-CMT-RMV by setting registry value 'PreXPSP2ShellProtocolBehavior' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\Explorer' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_MLA_EVC `Windows Server implements KSI-MLA-EVC by setting registry value 'PreXPSP2ShellProtocolBehavior' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\Explorer' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_SVC_ACM `Windows Server implements KSI-SVC-ACM by setting registry value 'PreXPSP2ShellProtocolBehavior' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\Explorer' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_CM_6 `Windows Server implements CM-6 by setting registry value 'PreXPSP2ShellProtocolBehavior' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\Explorer' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\Explorer`
        name `PreXPSP2ShellProtocolBehavior`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 0
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
